NAME
    rm - remove one or more regular files

SYNOPSIS
    rm FILE [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
    Unlinks each FILE. Reports per-file failures to stderr and keeps
    going — a missing FILE doesn't abort the rest. Exit status is 1
    only if at least one removal failed.

    Refuses directories. Use rmdir for empty dirs; there is no
    recursive rm -r in this OS yet.

    The kernel sys_unlink enforces:
      - owner-or-root permission on the target
      - refusal if any task currently has the file open (EBUSY-ish)
      - refusal on directories

EXAMPLES
    rm hello.txt
    rm /tmp/a.log /tmp/b.log /tmp/c.log

EXIT STATUS
    0   every FILE was removed
    1   at least one FILE could not be removed

SEE ALSO
    rmdir(1), find(1)

NOTES
    No -f (suppress errors), -i (interactive), or -r (recursive).
